Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.32,0:03:22.82,Episode Title,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,500,6000,7000)\pos(653.755,463.855)}Episode 48\N\N\N\N\NZhāng Sōng Presents a Map
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.66,0:03:29.26,Thinking,,0,0,0,,In the 16th year of the Jiàn'ān era (211 CE),
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.46,0:03:34.82,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Cao Cao decisively defeated Ma Chao of Western Liang. Hanzhong was greatly shaken.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.54,0:03:38.78,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Zhang Lu, fearing that Cao Cao would invade Hanzhong,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.90,0:03:45.22,Thinking,,0,0,0,,prepared to attack the Western Riverlands to gain a foothold to contend with Cao Cao.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.18,0:03:48.66,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Upon hearing this, Liu Zhang, Lord of Yi Province,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.70,0:03:52.58,Thinking,,0,0,0,,assembled the civil and military officials to discuss a countermeasure.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.10,0:03:58.02,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Zhang Song, the Aide-de-Camp of Yi, volunteered to be an envoy to Xudu,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.02,0:04:02.80,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(318.618,462.576)}Zhāng Sōng\NStyled: Yǒngnián
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.10,0:04:02.42,Thinking,,0,0,0,,claiming to negotiate with Cao Cao for Liu Zhang to attack Zhang Lu,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.54,0:04:08.78,Thinking,,0,0,0,,but in reality, he prepared to realize \Nhis long-cherished wish with this opportunity.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.72,0:04:17.68,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(292.364,473.741)}Cáo Cāo\NStyled: Mèngdé
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.56,0:04:35.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Who allowed you to rebuild this gate?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.82,0:04:36.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Speak.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.26,0:04:38.36,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(913.94,469.06)}Yáng Xiū\NStyled: Dézǔ
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.68,0:04:41.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Wasn't it Your Excellency who ordered us to do that?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.08,0:04:51.71,Default,,0,0,0,,When have I said this to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.98,0:05:01.16,Default,,0,0,0,,On the day when Chancellor came to the garden to see this gate,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.32,0:05:04.10,Default,,0,0,0,,you wrote the character for "alive" on the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.36,0:05:06.92,Default,,0,0,0,,The craftsmen did not understand its meaning.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.02,0:05:12.40,Default,,0,0,0,,It was I who told them that the character for "alive" within the character for "gate" is...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.42,0:05:14.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.68,0:05:18.26,Default,,0,0,0,,It was Registrar Yang Xiu, Lord Yang who instructed me,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.18,0:05:23.30,Default,,0,0,0,,saying that the character for "alive"(活) within the character for "gate"(門) means "wide"(闊).
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.26,0:05:33.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Excellency meant that the gate was wide,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.36,0:05:36.38,Default,,0,0,0,,and that narrowing it would make it look beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.40,0:05:38.44,Default,,0,0,0,,For this, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.14,0:05:54.42,Default,,0,0,0,,How astute you are, Dezu. How astute you are!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.62,0:05:56.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, you praise me too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.77,0:05:59.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.16,0:06:01.30,Default,,0,0,0,,What is the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.82,0:06:07.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, an emissary from Yi Province requests an audience. He is waiting at the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.10,0:06:16.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I have been on the saddle so long, I seldom have time for small joys,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.44,0:06:18.96,Default,,0,0,0,,but that lout Liu Zhang has come to spoil my rest too.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.44,0:06:24.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Who is this emissary?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.10,0:06:28.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhang Song, styled Yongnian, aide-de-camp of Yi Province.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.50,0:06:29.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Aide-de-Camp?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.56,0:06:33.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you good sirs heard of this man?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.80,0:06:35.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Never heard of him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.58,0:06:40.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Send him to a guesthouse and treat him well.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.88,0:06:41.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.52,0:06:43.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.74,0:06:47.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, the emissary from the Western Riverlands has come here from afar.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.82,0:06:52.18,Default,,0,0,0,,If you meet with him before all else, it could win the hearts of the West...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.32,0:06:55.46,Default,,0,0,0,,He has waited in the guesthouse for many days, why not-
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.18,0:06:56.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.96,0:07:00.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Summon the emissary from the Riverlands.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.18,0:07:02.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.82,0:07:45.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Lord, Liu Zhang, has not been paying tribute for all these years.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.82,0:07:48.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Why is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.88,0:07:54.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Roads are arduous and the bandits are wreaking havoc. It's too difficult to travel.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.14,0:07:59.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I have cleared out the Central Plains. \NHow could there be bandits?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.02,0:08:01.82,Default,,0,0,0,,In Jiangnan, there is Sun Quan.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.94,0:08:03.84,Default,,0,0,0,,In Hanzhong, there is Zhang Lu.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.90,0:08:05.66,Default,,0,0,0,,In Jīng Province, there is Liu Bei.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.78,0:08:11.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone is fighting against each other. \NHmph, how can you say there is peace?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.30,0:08:38.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, you are an emissary, how could you not know etiquette?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.38,0:08:40.34,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,What etiquette?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.36,0:08:43.34,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,That is the Chancellor. He is below one man and above ten thousand.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.42,0:08:44.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Not Liu Zhang of the Riverlands.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.06,0:08:49.38,Default,,0,0,0,,All conversations must be respectful, mannerly, careful, and humble.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.84,0:08:55.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}There are hundreds of thousands of people in the Western Riverlands,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.86,0:08:58.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}and none of them are cowering petty men who cajole and fawn.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.26,0:08:58.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,604)}You...!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.55,0:08:59.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,604)}Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.26,0:09:02.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}If the Riverlands have no petty men,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.46,0:09:04.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}are they all in the Central Plains then?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.98,0:09:07.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Who is this man?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.86,0:09:10.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor's Registrar Yang Xiu, Lord Yang.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.42,0:09:14.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}I am ignorant and ill-informed,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.74,0:09:18.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}knowing little of Shu's customs and practices.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.74,0:09:18.10,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Shǔ (蜀) corresponds to modern Sichuan-province
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.10,0:09:21.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}I wonder if you, sir, could grant me a teaching or two?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.56,0:09:29.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Shu, or Yi Province, long known as the Garden of Heaven.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.20,0:09:33.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Protected by the arduous Jin River, {\bord12}\Nand the indomitable terrain of Jiange.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.02,0:09:36.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}The circuit is 280 journeys long,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.47,0:09:39.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}and the perimeter more than 30,000 {\i1}li.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.98,0:09:42.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}The land is teeming with clucks of chicken and barks of dogs.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.98,0:09:46.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}The fields are fertile, the land rich, and the people prosperous.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.30,0:09:51.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}No sight of flood or drought, only sounds of instruments abound.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.61,0:09:55.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}What can be made can pile up like mountains,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.86,0:10:01.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}which is unparalleled in the world!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.50,0:10:07.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}May I ask what the people of Shu are like?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.40,0:10:09.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}With the pen, there is poetry like that of Sima Changqing;
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.38,0:10:09.86,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Referring to Sīmǎ Xiàngrú (司馬相如), a famed poet and musician of the Western Hàn Dynasty. Famous for his {\i1}fù{\i0} (赋)-rhapsodies.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.86,0:10:11.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}with the sword, talent like that of Ma Fubo;
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.86,0:10:11.48,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Mǎ Yuán (馬援), a general who fought under Liu Xiu and helped establish the Eastern Han Dynasty. Famously battled the Trưng sisters of Vietnam
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.48,0:10:13.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}in medicine, skill like that of Zhang Zhongjing;
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.48,0:10:13.40,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Zhāng Jī (张机), a pharmacologist and physician who greatly contributed to Traditional Chinese Medicine. Alive at the time of this conversation.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.40,0:10:16.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}in divination, profoundness like Yan Junping.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.40,0:10:16.10,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Yán Zūn ((严遵), a Taoist scholar and philosopher of the Western Hàn Dynasty. Known as one of the Eight Immortals of Shǔ (蜀之八仙), along with Laozi, Dong Zhongshu, and Li Babai.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.30,0:10:21.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Among the Three Teachings and the Nine Schools, \Nthe exemplary, and the outstanding are incalculable,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.30,0:10:24.06,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,"Three Teachings": Religious Confucianism, Taoism, and Buddhism.\N"Nine Schools": Ruism, Daoism, Naturalism, Legalism, Logicians, Mohism, Diplomatists, Syncretism and Agriculturalism.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.80,0:10:24.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}and, therefore, innumerable.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.99,0:10:31.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}May I ask, among the officials of Lord Liu of Shu, how many more are like you, sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.65,0:10:36.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Those with talents in pen and sword, with wisdom and bravery,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.94,0:10:40.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}and who are both just and generous number in the hundreds.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.94,0:10:47.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}As for lesser people like me, there are cartloads.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.18,0:10:54.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}May I ask what position you hold, sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.22,0:10:59.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}A sham of an aide-de-camp. Nothing notable.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.84,0:11:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}May I ask what position you, sir, have in the Imperial Court?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.90,0:11:13.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}I am a registrar in the Chancellor's Office.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.20,0:11:21.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}I have heard that you are of noble pedigree.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.18,0:11:24.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Why not serve the Son of Heaven in the Court,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.04,0:11:28.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}rather than lower yourself to being \Na mere registrar under the Chancellor?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.88,0:11:36.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Though I am a lowly official,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.02,0:11:40.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Chancellor has given me the great task of managing military and administration.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.70,0:11:45.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}I am being educated day and night, and I have learned much.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.88,0:11:50.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}For this, I willingly serve in the Chancellor's Office.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.79,0:12:02.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}According to what I have heard,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.28,0:12:05.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Chancellor Cao knows not the ways of Confucius and Mencius,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.58,0:12:07.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}reaches not the skill of Sun Wu and Wu Qi,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.62,0:12:08.68,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Sūn Wǔ (孙武) AKA. Sun Tzu, General of the Spring and Autumn period who served the state of Wu. \NWú Qǐ (吴起), General and politician of the Warring States, whose reforms that greatly strengthened the state of Chǔ.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.56,0:12:11.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}and sits on his position by brute force.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.60,0:12:15.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}How could he educate you, sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.60,0:12:19.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}You, sir, live in the hinterlands.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.28,0:12:22.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}How could you know of the Chancellor's talent?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.74,0:12:35.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Please look, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.08,0:13:26.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you, sir, know what book this is?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.10,0:13:32.80,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the hard work of the Chancellor,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.06,0:13:36.58,Default,,0,0,0,,a treatise on war, in following of Sun Tzu's thirteen chapters.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.28,0:13:36.60,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,AKA. {\i1}The Art of War
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.96,0:13:38.84,Default,,0,0,0,,You said that Chancellor is talentless.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.88,0:13:41.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Is not a book worthy of being passed into posterity?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.90,0:13:56.54,Default,,0,0,0,,This book was written by an anonymous man of the Warring States.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.68,0:13:59.72,Default,,0,0,0,,In Shu, even children three {\i1}chi{\i0} short can recite it,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.66,0:14:00.92,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,1 {\i1}chǐ{\i0} (尺)≈ 24cm during the Eastern Hàn Dynasty.\N1 {\i1}chǐ{\i0} (尺)≈ 31cm when {\i1}Romance of the Three Kingdoms{\i0} was written.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.84,0:14:03.22,Default,,0,0,0,,but Chancellor Cao stole it for himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.30,0:14:08.30,Default,,0,0,0,,That can fool nobody but you, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.88,0:14:18.70,Default,,0,0,0,,This is Chancellor's secret draft and has not been made public yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.10,0:14:24.66,Default,,0,0,0,,You say that even children in Shu can recite it...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.70,0:14:29.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Isn't that claim a bit too tall, sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.14,0:14:35.32,Default,,0,0,0,,If you, sir, do not believe me, I can recite it to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.47,0:14:38.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Let us hear it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.27,0:14:52.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}In the past, Sun Tzu had saith: \N"The art of war is of vital importance to the State."
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.56,0:14:55.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}"It is a matter of life and death, \Na road either to safety or to ruin."
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.98,0:14:58.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,669.667)}"Hence it is an inquiry not to be neglected."
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.98,0:15:11.32,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,From {\i1}Notes of Sun Tzu's Art of War{\i0} (孙子略解), by Cáo Cāo.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.51,0:15:02.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Military has no constant force, \Nas water has no constant shape.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.16,0:15:06.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Changes on the field must \Nnot be divulged beforehand.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.64,0:15:11.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Thus, anticipating the enemy lies in the heart, and finding opportunities lies in the eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.94,0:15:22.60,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sūn Bìn's Art of War{\i0} (孙膑兵法), Audience with King Wēi (见威王). Edited from translation by Ralph D. Sawyer.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.54,0:15:16.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Thus, wars are not to be taken pleasure in, \Nvictory is not to be sought profit from.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.44,0:15:19.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}{\pos(640,664)}One who takes pleasure in war will perish,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.37,0:15:22.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}one who finds profit in victory will be humiliated.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.14,0:15:26.84,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sūn Bìn's Art of War, Lunar Warfare (月战). Edited from translation by Ralph D. Sawyer.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.44,0:15:26.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}In between Heaven and Earth nothing is more noble than man.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.96,0:15:32.56,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Works of Mencius{\i0}: Gōng Sūn Chǒu II (公孙丑下). Edited from translation by James Legge.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.96,0:15:32.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Mencius saith: "Heaven-sent Chances are lesser to Benefits of Earth, lesser still to the Union of Men."
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.24,0:15:38.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Victory against all without these three is a matter unheard of by any.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.28,0:15:42.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Rule the state with trust and the army with deceit, as none mirror the other.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.64,0:15:46.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}As armies deny the state, the state denies the army; thus Rites and Etiquette are unfit to command.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.76,0:15:49.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}The soldiers' profit lies in trust; their morality in principle.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.27,0:15:52.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Let morals be grown in time; \Nlet trust be rewarded in largesse.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.72,0:15:54.91,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,From {\i1}Notes of Sun Tzu's Art of War{\i0} (孙子略解), by Cáo Cāo.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.66,0:15:54.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Men will not come for no wealth, nor move without reward.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.93,0:16:08.32,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sūn Bìn's Art of War{\i0} (孙膑兵法): Expanding Ch’i (延气). Edited from translation by Ralph D. Sawyer.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.74,0:15:57.83,Default,,0,0,0,,To muster crowds one must incite their fervor. To face an enemy one must hone that fervor.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.83,0:16:00.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Till the day of war, abate that fervor; \Nwith war ongoing, swell their fervor.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.10,0:16:00.98,Default,,0,0,0,,-Sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.98,0:16:03.24,Default,,0,0,0,,For absent fervor is dullness, dullness leads to errors. To err is to suffer.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.24,0:16:06.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Fervor unhoned leads to fear. In fear men swarm in frenzy and cowardice, which leads...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.25,0:16:04.20,Default,,0,0,0,,-Sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.19,0:16:06.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.18,0:16:07.24,Default,,0,0,0,,... To Death!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.26,0:16:12.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Enough! Enough!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.82,0:16:18.78,Default,,0,0,0,,You, sir, possess total recall. What a prodigy below Heaven!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.54,0:16:24.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Today has been eye-opening for me. I offer great respect.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.78,0:16:30.34,Default,,0,0,0,,It was but a small trick. \NHow could I accept such excessive praise?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.42,0:16:35.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Please do not be overly modest, sir. \NMy words are sincere.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.56,0:16:37.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Please wait at the guesthouse, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.54,0:16:41.86,Default,,0,0,0,,After I petition the Chancellor, he will certainly grant an audience with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.94,0:16:43.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you for taking the trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.46,0:16:47.34,Default,,0,0,0,,-Farewell.\N-Pardon me for not sending you off.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.38,0:17:02.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Why say more? This man is ugly in countenance and crazed in speech.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.78,0:17:04.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Truly, a despicable man!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.94,0:17:07.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}In the past, Mi Heng was far more crazed and arrogant,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.14,0:17:10.68,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Mí Héng (祢衡) was a writer and musician of the late Eastern Han Dynasty. \NFamous for his temperament, he had insulted and humiliated Cao Cao many times.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.18,0:17:10.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}yet Chancellor tolerated him.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.72,0:17:14.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Why not show tolerance to Zhang Song who came from afar.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.06,0:17:24.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Mi Heng's writing exceeds all else, his name was acclaimed by all.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.28,0:17:28.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Zhang Song is but a nameless baseborn.\NHow can he compare to Mi Heng?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.66,0:17:35.46,Default,,0,0,0,,In my opinion, Zhang Song's talent is no less than that of Mi Heng.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.26,0:17:42.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Not only is this man makes convincing arguments and is eloquent in speech,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.18,0:17:47.02,Default,,0,0,0,,his total recall is rare in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.86,0:17:49.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Total recall?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.37,0:17:54.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I allowed Zhang Song to witness Chancellor's great talent,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.02,0:17:57.10,Default,,0,0,0,,by giving him this draft to read.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.30,0:18:03.50,Default,,0,0,0,,To my surprise, after this man browsed it once, he could recite it without a single error.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.74,0:18:08.82,Default,,0,0,0,,This I saw myself and heard myself:
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.94,0:18:11.54,Default,,0,0,0,,not a single bit of falsehood.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.42,0:18:22.98,Default,,0,0,0,,He deliberately mystified the manner,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.06,0:18:27.42,Default,,0,0,0,,by saying that this book was written by a nameless man of the Warring States,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.70,0:18:30.54,Default,,0,0,0,,and that even children of Shu can recite it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.82,0:18:39.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Surely...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.55,0:18:43.35,Default,,0,0,0,,the words of ancient men do not coincide with my own?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.00,0:18:47.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Attend me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.50,0:18:50.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.38,0:18:55.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.34,0:19:29.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.26,0:20:30.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Chancellor has put great effort into writing this book.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.14,0:20:33.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}This sweat and blood of twenty years,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.78,0:20:38.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}why, for a couple of foolish words, destroy it so utterly?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.04,0:20:46.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Rather than leave a soiled name for generations to come,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.36,0:20:50.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}I would burn it myself first.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.98,0:21:01.34,Default,,0,0,0,,If Zhang Song indeed has extraordinary talent,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.50,0:21:05.66,Default,,0,0,0,,during tomorrow's army review, you can bring him to meet me.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.94,0:21:09.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Let him see the grandeur of our army,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.62,0:21:12.38,Default,,0,0,0,,and tell him to go back and say this:
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.66,0:21:18.46,Default,,0,0,0,,after I descend upon Jiangnan, I will take the Western Riverlands.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.58,0:21:20.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.50,0:22:16.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.80,0:22:49.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Sir, you have the capability of total recall,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.32,0:22:56.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}and I have the capacity to care for the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.64,0:23:00.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Chancellor's talents are akin to \Nswallowing the sky and the ground,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.95,0:23:06.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}and the will to encompass all Four Directions. \NHow dare I compare?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.07,0:23:15.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Have you seen this sort of formation in the Riverlands?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.72,0:23:17.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}I have never.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.96,0:23:21.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}In the Riverlands, we have only valued benevolence,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.22,0:23:23.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}what use is there for soldiers such as these?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.04,0:23:51.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}I oversee the world with pride.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:53.72,0:23:58.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Wherever my army goes, their smite is not followed by plunder, nor defeat.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.66,0:24:01.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Those who obey me live, and those who defy me die.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:01.38,0:24:03.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Do you know this?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.70,0:24:09.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Hmph. How can I, Zhang Song, not know of Chancellor's tiger-like prowess?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.14,0:24:13.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Such as the time of Lü Bu at Puyang,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.80,0:24:16.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}the day of battling Zhang Xiu at Wancheng,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:16.94,0:24:21.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}meeting Zhou the Youth at Chibi, \Nfacing Guan Yu at the Huarong road,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.10,0:24:24.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}cutting beard and discarding robe at Tong Pass,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:24.80,0:24:27.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Stealing boats and fleeing from arrows on Wei River.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:28.10,0:24:31.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Oh, truly invincible and undefeated!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:32.86,0:24:33.98,Default,,0,0,0,,How dare you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:38.98,0:24:43.06,Default,,0,0,0,,A mere petty scholar dares to debate failures with me?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:44.34,0:24:45.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Men!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:45.86,0:24:47.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-Yes, sir.\N-Seize him!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:53.62,0:24:56.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Push him out and behead him.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:03.86,0:25:10.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}To think I, Zhang Song, could fall to treachery as well!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:14.94,0:25:19.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor! Zhang Song came here from Shu to pay tribute.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:19.82,0:25:23.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Executing him may lose the hearts of the borderlands.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:23.54,0:25:27.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope that Chancellor can show him leniency.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:29.18,0:25:31.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, please rest your anger!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:32.02,0:25:35.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Dezu's words are correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:34.80,0:25:36.86,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(961.916,529.939)}Xún Yù\NStyled: \NWénruò
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.72,0:25:38.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope that Chancellor reconsiders.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:48.20,0:25:52.30,Default,,0,0,0,,If it is not for the loyal heart of your master Liu Zhang,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:52.98,0:25:54.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I would kill you here and now!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:56.74,0:25:58.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Beat him out of the drill grounds!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:11.34,0:26:14.70,Default,,0,0,0,,My Lord, Zhang Song was driven out, and left Xudu overnight.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:15.74,0:26:17.62,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(253.798,276.364)}Zhūgě Liàng\NStyled: \NKǒngmíng
Dialogue: 0,0:26:16.02,0:26:16.98,Default,,0,0,0,,As expected.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:18.52,0:26:21.22,Default,,0,0,0,,-Good. Go and get your reward.\N-Thank you, Strategos!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:21.86,0:26:24.66,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(978.863,521.696)}Páng Tǒng\NStyled: \NShìyuán
Dialogue: 0,0:26:22.26,0:26:23.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Shìyuán.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:28.42,0:26:32.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Truly, my Lord is greatly blessed by Heaven.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:32.98,0:26:38.25,Default,,0,0,0,,What are the two Strategists laughing about? I am not in the know, so please explain.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:34.26,0:26:36.68,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(290.002,519.637)}Liú Bèi\NStyled: Xuándé
Dialogue: 0,0:26:39.72,0:26:44.22,Default,,0,0,0,,My Lord still lacks the Western Riverlands' \NBenefits of Earth and Union of Men.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:44.28,0:26:50.46,Default,,0,0,0,,However, it seems its acquisition will now fall on this man, driven out of Xudu by Cao Cao,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:50.54,0:26:52.94,Default,,0,0,0,,this aide-de-camp of the Western Riverlands!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:55.00,0:26:58.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Call Zǐlong and Yunchang for a conference.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:58.30,0:26:58.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:15.40,0:27:18.86,Thinking,,0,0,0,,I thought I could find an enlightened lord and present the Riverlands to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:18.87,0:27:21.78,Thinking,,0,0,0,,But that arrogant Cao Cao is dismissive of the wise and capable.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.78,0:27:24.70,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Before the trip, I boasted to Liu Zhang
Dialogue: 0,0:27:24.74,0:27:28.78,Thinking,,0,0,0,,that I could persuade Cao Cao and end the threat of Zhang Lu.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:28.79,0:27:30.72,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Now, I return empty-handed.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:30.72,0:27:34.14,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Will I not be ridiculed by the people of Shu?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:38.62,0:27:41.02,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(959.251,506.787)}Zhào Yún\NStyled: Zǐlóng
Dialogue: 0,0:27:44.42,0:27:46.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you Aide-de-Camp Zhang of Yi Province?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:47.66,0:27:48.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Indeed I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:00.90,0:28:04.60,Default,,0,0,0,,May I have your names, Generals? What is it you want?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:05.18,0:28:08.56,Default,,0,0,0,,I am Guan Yu. On the orders of my Lord, Liu Xuande,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:08.66,0:28:12.72,Default,,0,0,0,,the guesthouse has been prepared\N and awaits Your Excellency's arrival.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:14.14,0:28:18.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I, Zhao Yun, on the orders of Strategos, \Nhave set up a banquet for Your Excellency.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:19.82,0:28:24.42,Default,,0,0,0,,You two are the world-renowned Zilong and Yunchang?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:24.66,0:28:25.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:25.22,0:28:27.36,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(323.507,282.424)}Guān Yǔ\NStyled: \NYúncháng
Dialogue: 0,0:28:27.26,0:28:28.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Please mount, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:28.50,0:28:31.98,Default,,0,0,0,,My Lord and the two Strategists are waiting for you, sir, just ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.54,0:28:35.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Liu Bei, the Imperial Uncle.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:37.34,0:28:40.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Wòlóng{\i0}, {\i1}Fèngchú{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:29:09.20,0:29:12.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}I have never before been acquainted with Imperial Uncle Liu,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.76,0:29:15.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}and was only passing by. \NHow can I accept this great kindness?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:16.78,0:29:20.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}I have long heard of your esteemed name, Aide-de-Camp, but never could meet with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:20.76,0:29:23.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Today, I heard that you were returning to Shu.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.06,0:29:26.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}If you would like, please rest a while at Huangzhou,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:26.25,0:29:28.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}so that we can discuss my thoughts of respect.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:29.20,0:29:33.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Imperial Uncle's benevolence is known far and wide. I have long admired you.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:33.44,0:29:38.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}However, to make such an imposition, I am greatly ashamed!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:39.02,0:29:42.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Excellency need not be modest. Please, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:42.14,0:29:44.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Imperial Uncle, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:44.42,0:29:46.54,Default,,0,0,0,,-Aide-de-Camp, please.\N-Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:50.18,0:29:55.22,Default,,0,0,0,,-Please look, sir, the scenery here is excellent.\N-Very good!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:55.30,0:29:57.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Why make a big fuss like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:57.62,0:30:00.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Strategos' reckoning is not what you or I can anticipate.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:18.46,0:30:19.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:21.38,0:30:23.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Imperial Uncle, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:29.22,0:30:31.42,Default,,0,0,0,,May I ask, Aide-de-Camp, of your age?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:32.26,0:30:35.74,Default,,0,0,0,,In front of Imperial Uncle, my age is of no significance.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:35.84,0:30:38.04,Default,,0,0,0,,How many sons and daughters?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:38.08,0:30:39.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Only one son.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:39.58,0:30:43.54,Default,,0,0,0,,What a coincidence! I, too, have only one son.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:46.10,0:30:48.38,Default,,0,0,0,,What is the age of your esteemed son?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:51.34,0:30:53.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Five years.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:55.70,0:31:00.54,Default,,0,0,0,,My son is five years old as well. Is it not a happenstance arranged by Heaven?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:02.30,0:31:05.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, what a coincidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:08.86,0:31:12.22,Default,,0,0,0,,-Aide-de-Camp, please.\N-Imperial Uncle, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:22.66,0:31:24.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:30.66,0:31:32.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:51.66,0:31:55.94,Default,,0,0,0,,-Please, sir.\N-Oh, I dare not, I dare not.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:05.66,0:32:07.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, your hand...?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:11.54,0:32:15.70,Default,,0,0,0,,A scrape due to a jolt on horseback.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:18.90,0:32:23.22,Default,,0,0,0,,It is a chaotic world, you need to be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:31.47,0:32:35.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Imperial Uncle, great in virtue, shall pacify this chaotic world,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:36.07,0:32:37.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}and unify the Four Seas.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:44.51,0:32:47.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}I wonder, sir, as you garrison Jing Province,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:47.64,0:32:50.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}how many Commanderies are under your jurisdiction?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:52.96,0:32:55.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Jing Province was to belong to Eastern Wu,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:55.42,0:32:57.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}and now serves as my Lord's shelter.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:58.54,0:33:02.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}They send people regularly to demand it back. How troublesome!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:05.98,0:33:09.87,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,This is a figurative expression. Provinces were greater than commanderies at that time, and it was not possible to have more provinces than commanderies.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:05.98,0:33:05.98,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,SARRACENIAN NOTE: The "Six commanderies and eighty-one provinces" was likely an error made by Luo Guanzhong for mistaking and mixing up the Ming Dynasty way of dividing lands with how it's divided in the Eastern Han. In the Ming Dynasty "州" is a lesser subdivision, somewhat equivalent to a county, so I figure to change it to "eighty-one counties", though technically in history, Wu does have Less or MORE counties than 81, depending on whether you count only the principal administrative county of each commandery, or in raw numbers of counties. Eastern Wu, even before attaining Jiaozhou, let alone Jingzhou, would have more than six commanderies.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:05.98,0:33:09.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Eastern Wú occupies six commanderies and eighty-one provinces,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.70,0:33:11.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}and it is still not content?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:11.90,0:33:14.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}My Lord is an Imperial Uncle of the Great Han,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:14.60,0:33:16.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}but cannot occupy provinces and commanderies.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:16.74,0:33:20.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Those brigands to the Han, however, encroach on land with force.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:21.10,0:33:22.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}It is infuriating!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:23.50,0:33:26.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Now now, let us not go too far.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:26.86,0:33:32.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}What merit do I have to dare make such an improper thought?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:32.07,0:33:35.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Imperial Uncle, you are a kin of the Han, spreading benevolence far and wide.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:35.83,0:33:40.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}You have the right to claim legitimacy and vie for the imperial throne, let alone occupy land!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:40.63,0:33:42.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Is that not true?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:42.87,0:33:44.30,Default,,0,0,0,,These words are untrue!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:44.58,0:33:47.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I would not dream of it!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:55.82,0:33:59.42,Thinking,,0,0,0,,During tomorrow's parting, I will make a closer examination of him,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:59.50,0:34:03.30,Thinking,,0,0,0,,see whether he treats me with sincerity or if he has an ulterior motive.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:03.38,0:34:08.08,Thinking,,0,0,0,,I hope that the Riverlands can be fortunate, that I can be fortunate, for this trip not to be in vain.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:17.38,0:34:21.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, no need to send me off.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:21.62,0:34:28.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you for your kindness, sir. You have stayed in Huangzhou for three days, for which I am honored.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:33.82,0:34:39.94,Default,,0,0,0,,With this cup of wine, I, Liu Bei, express my admiration. Please drink it all, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:49.14,0:34:53.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, I will never forget your erudition and talent for my entire life.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:53.74,0:34:59.38,Default,,0,0,0,,With this cup of wine, I wish you, sir, a brilliant future with all aspirations rewarded.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:01.54,0:35:03.99,Thinking,,0,0,0,,With all aspirations rewarded.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:14.06,0:35:17.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, my Lord, for the grace of healing my injury.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:20.98,0:35:27.06,Default,,0,0,0,,With this third cup of wine, I wish you, sir, a safe journey.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:27.54,0:35:29.42,Default,,0,0,0,,After this parting,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:29.86,0:35:37.42,Default,,0,0,0,,with passes and mountains being numerous, I do not know when I may see you again.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:06.74,0:36:11.22,Default,,0,0,0,,My Lord, send the aide-de-camp on his way.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:21.49,0:36:24.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, your hand injury is not yet healed.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:24.97,0:36:28.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Allow me, Liu Bei, to lead the horse and hold the stirrup.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:33.70,0:36:36.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:39.66,0:36:42.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:50.26,0:36:52.82,Default,,0,0,0,,My Lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:56.66,0:36:58.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, please rise.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:01.50,0:37:03.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, please rise.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:06.18,0:37:08.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}{\pos(640,664)}How compassionate and caring you are, my Lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:08.74,0:37:11.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}I wish I could be by your side day and night.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:11.74,0:37:13.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Sadly, I have no opportunity to do so.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:14.18,0:37:17.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}I offer a word upon today's parting.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:17.56,0:37:21.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}If there is any offense, I hope that you, sir, can pardon me.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:21.64,0:37:23.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}I listen to your wisdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:23.24,0:37:24.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}In my observation,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:24.56,0:37:27.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Jing Province, though protected by water and terrain,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:27.44,0:37:32.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}has Sun Quan to the east and Cao Cao to the north, both vying for conquest!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:32.82,0:37:37.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}It cannot serve as a sanctuary for long.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:42.61,0:37:44.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}I, too, know of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:46.12,0:37:52.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Sadly, the realm, with all its greatness, still does not offer a place for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:52.60,0:37:56.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Yi Province is a vast, fertile land, \Nrich in wealth and prosperity.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:56.16,0:37:59.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Its great gentry have long admired your benevolence, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:59.86,0:38:04.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Should you raise the troops of Jing and march west, then your hegemony could be built,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:04.42,0:38:06.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}and the Han Dynasty can rise again!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:08.34,0:38:12.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Aide-de-Camp, I have accepted your kindness with my heart,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:13.38,0:38:16.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}but Liu Zhang of Yi Province is, too, a kin of the imperial clan.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:18.31,0:38:20.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}How can I take it from my kin?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:20.84,0:38:22.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Incorrect, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:22.33,0:38:25.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}I, Zhang Song, am not selling my lord out for glory,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:25.05,0:38:26.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}but, meeting you, sir, today,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:26.89,0:38:30.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}I must be frank and sincere.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:30.58,0:38:32.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Liu Jiyu is weak and incapable,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:32.26,0:38:34.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}{\pos(640,664)}and with Zhang Lu to the north intending to invade.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:35.05,0:38:39.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Should you not seize it, the land will belong to another sooner or later.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:40.06,0:38:42.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}At that point, will it not be too late to regret?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:42.76,0:38:44.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Rather than leaving it to beasts,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:44.65,0:38:48.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}I would rather give it to a virtuous lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:49.21,0:38:52.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Hearing your words is akin to \Na light brought to the darkness.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:52.58,0:38:55.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}However, the paths of Shu are treacherous, unfit for horses and carriages.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:56.02,0:38:58.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Even if I had the intent to take the Riverlands,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:58.50,0:39:00.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}I would be helpless!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:05.70,0:39:10.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}All of Shu's mountains, rivers, roads, valleys, bridges, passes, and treasuries
Dialogue: 0,0:39:10.12,0:39:12.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}are all drawn onto this map by me, one by one.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:12.40,0:39:14.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Now, I offer it to you, sir,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:14.94,0:39:17.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}to repay the kindness of your patronage!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:23.94,0:39:27.22,Default,,0,0,0,,You had this map drawn by memory in three days?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:29.46,0:39:32.85,Default,,0,0,0,,To speak frankly, during my trip to Xudu,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:32.85,0:39:37.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I intended to give this map to Cao Cao, to aid him in taking Shu.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:37.28,0:39:40.46,Default,,0,0,0,,But that Cao Cao bullies the virtuous and slights the noble.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:40.50,0:39:42.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I was greatly disappointed.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:42.46,0:39:45.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, with gratitude, I gift this map.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:45.50,0:39:47.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Take the Riverlands as the foundation,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:47.25,0:39:49.64,Default,,0,0,0,,aim for Hanzhong to the north, and retake the Central Plains
Dialogue: 0,0:39:49.64,0:39:53.78,Default,,0,0,0,,so that the Celestial Reign may be righted, and your name may go down in history.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:59.54,0:40:05.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I bid farewell.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:37.62,0:40:43.78,Default,,0,0,0,,My Lord, I have a plan that can deter Cao Cao and Zhang Lu from attacking the Western Riverlands.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:47.82,0:40:49.13,Default,,0,0,0,,What plan?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:49.13,0:40:53.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Imperial Uncle Liu of Jing Province is of the same clan as Your Excellency, and is kind and generous.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:53.32,0:40:58.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Why not send an envoy to express goodwill, so that he may come and aid us?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:00.34,0:41:02.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I have also thought of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:02.31,0:41:07.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Fa Zheng can be the envoy, to invite Imperial Uncle Liu to enter the Riverlands.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:08.02,0:41:12.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, send Meng Da with five thousand troops to welcome him.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:15.94,0:41:21.50,Default,,0,0,0,,My Lord, Liu Zhang's invitation of entering the Riverlands with troops
Dialogue: 0,0:41:21.73,0:41:24.24,Default,,0,0,0,,is truly a Heaven-granted opportunity.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:26.24,0:41:28.24,Default,,0,0,0,,With Zhang Song giving the map,
Dialogue: 0,0:41:29.60,0:41:32.18,Default,,0,0,0,,and Fa Zheng being our inside man,
Dialogue: 0,0:41:32.32,0:41:37.06,Default,,0,0,0,,the Heaven-Sent Chance, the Benefits of Earth, and the Union of Men are all in place.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:39.62,0:41:42.82,Default,,0,0,0,,My Lord, why be indecisive?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:44.32,0:41:45.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Right now,
Dialogue: 0,0:41:45.94,0:41:48.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}only Cao Cao is against me like water and fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:50.94,0:41:53.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}While he is irascible, I am lenient.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:53.86,0:41:56.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}While he is cruel, I am kind.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:57.04,0:41:59.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}While he fosters duplicity, I foster loyalty.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:59.64,0:42:03.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Whenever I do the opposite of Cao Cao, I have accomplished much.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:03.58,0:42:07.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Today, Liu Jiyu and I have the relation of kin,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:07.78,0:42:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}and he has invited me sincerely.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:10.04,0:42:12.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}If I seize the Western Riverlands with this opportunity,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:13.74,0:42:18.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}I might lose the realm's trust. How can I bear to do this?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:18.88,0:42:22.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}My Lord, these words suit your divine justice,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:22.66,0:42:25.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}yet in today's corrupt and chaotic world,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:26.82,0:42:30.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}to command armies and fight for oneself demands adaptability.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:32.56,0:42:34.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Should common sense be clung to,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:34.86,0:42:38.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}it will certainly be difficult to move even a single step.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:39.54,0:42:43.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Now, Zhang Lu is coveting the Western Riverlands,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:43.78,0:42:46.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}and Liu Zhang is weak and incapable.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:48.44,0:42:53.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}My Lord, if you do not take it today, \Nit will fall to someone else tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:54.28,0:42:58.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Then, would it not be too late for regrets?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:04.64,0:43:08.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Annex the weak and attack the foolish, seize the stubborn and protect the docile.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:09.32,0:43:12.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}These were the ways of Tang of Shang and King Wu of Zhou.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:09.32,0:43:15.26,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Tāng of Shāng is the first king of the Shāng Dynasty, who overthrew Jie of Xia.\NKing Wǔ of Zhōu, the first king of the Zhōu Dynasty, overthrew the Shang.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:12.82,0:43:14.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}how will trust be breached then?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:15.61,0:43:20.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}After the deed is done, treat Liu Zhang kindly, and reward him handsomely with endowments and gifts.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:21.33,0:43:24.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}How will justice be violated then?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:26.42,0:43:29.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}Strategist's words of metal and stone, are etched onto my lungs and organs.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:29.83,0:43:31.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,664)}{\bord12}Now, my heart is much relieved.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:32.55,0:43:36.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}After tonight's banquet, let us invite Strategos Kongming and Fa Xiaozhi here,
Dialogue: 0,0:43:36.79,0:43:38.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}to discuss entering the Riverlands together!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:40.42,0:43:44.98,Thinking,,0,0,0,,In the winter of the 16th year of the Jiàn'ān era, winter of 211 CE,
Dialogue: 0,0:43:45.26,0:43:51.42,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Liu Bei requested Zhuge Liang, and commanded Guan Yu, Zhang Fei, and Zhao Yun to guard Jing Province,
Dialogue: 0,0:43:51.50,0:43:53.42,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,whereas he, together with Strategist Pang Tong,
Dialogue: 0,0:43:53.42,0:43:57.26,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,and Generals Huang Zhong, Wei Yan, Liu Feng, and Guan Ping,
Dialogue: 0,0:43:57.34,0:44:02.66,Thinking,,0,0,0,,lead a great army from Jing Province to the Western Riverlands.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:27.70,0:44:33.98,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}Dim grows the flashing of swords and daggers,
Dialogue: 0,0:44:33.98,0:44:39.30,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}from afar do sound the battle drums and war horns.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:39.68,0:44:46.10,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}Before my eyes rise only those
Dialogue: 0,0:44:46.10,0:44:51.70,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}fresh faces, one after another.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:52.20,0:44:58.43,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}Buried are the ancient paths and ways,
Dialogue: 0,0:44:58.43,0:45:03.74,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}desolate are the beacon fires and border towns.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:03.74,0:45:11.58,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}O, Years! You cannot take away
Dialogue: 0,0:45:11.58,0:45:15.75,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}that succession of familiar lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:16.73,0:45:22.86,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}Who is it that determines what flourishes?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:22.86,0:45:29.26,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}Is there no basis to prosperity and decline?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:29.26,0:45:35.22,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}In a single page, the storm disperses,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:35.22,0:45:41.30,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}reshaping space and time.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:41.30,0:45:47.62,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}Meeting and parting are always destined,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:47.62,0:45:53.70,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}separation and reunion always weighs in our hearts.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:53.70,0:45:59.70,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}Take the work of the living upon yourself,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:59.70,0:46:06.15,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}unconcerned with your legacy after.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:06.15,0:46:12.26,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}The Yangtze has the will to transform into tears,
Dialogue: 0,0:46:12.26,0:46:18.42,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12\pos(640,678.667)}the Yangtze has sentiment to raise its voice in song,
Dialogue: 0,0:46:18.42,0:46:24.54,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}in the firmament of history\N glimmers a sprinkling of stars,
Dialogue: 0,0:46:24.54,0:46:45.70,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord12}the spirit of heroism in the world\N thunders onward unbridled

